r=add(47,'Carrot Broth with Rice',8,90,'Sieved carrots flavor a light broth in which whole rice grains cook until tender.',[carrot(800),stock(2000),rice(80),salt()],['Put {{carrot}} in a saucepan with {{stock}} and {{salt}}. Keep small carrots whole, halving thick ones lengthwise. Cover and simmer for 40–60 minutes until very soft.',PUREE,'Rinse {{rice}}, add to the simmering soup and cook gently for 15–20 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the grains are tender. Add small splashes of hot water if the soup becomes too thick.'],'The extraction specifies rice grains, unlike the same-book rice-flour soup; this interpretation is retained as a distinct modern adaptation. Missing stock and rice amounts are supplied.','Soups')
r=add(114,'Enkel Morotpuré (Carrot, Leek and Bread Soup)',10,85,'Carrots and leeks simmer with bread for a lightly thickened soup, with toast served alongside.',[carrot(450),I('leek',300,'g','trimmed leeks, thoroughly rinsed','Use the same weight of onion.'),butter(28),stock(3000),bread(200),salt(),sugar(4),cayenne()],['Dice {{carrot}} and slice {{leek}}. Melt {{butter}} in a large saucepan and soften the vegetables for 5 minutes without browning.','Add {{stock|0.3333333333333333}} and {{bread|0.5}} cut into cubes. Cover and simmer for 1 hour, stirring occasionally, until the vegetables are very soft.',PUREE,'Add {{stock|0.6666666666666667}}, {{salt}}, {{sugar}} and {{cayenne}}. Bring to a gentle boil, skim any foam and stir well.','Toast {{bread|0.5}} until crisp and serve alongside.'],'The price-defined loaf becomes a disclosed 200 g bread portion, divided equally between soup and toast. Two leeks become 300 g trimmed weight. The alternative anchovy-butter accompaniment is preserved as a named version.','Soups')
