r=add(115,'Fin Morotpuré (Browned Carrot Soup with Cream)',9,65,'Browned carrots give a light, smooth soup finished with a cooked egg-yolk and cream liaison.',[carrot(500),butter(30),stock(2667),flour(10),salt(),dict(pepper(),name='ground white pepper'),yolks(2),cream(100)],['Dice {{carrot}}. Melt {{butter|0.5}} in a saucepan and sauté the carrots for 8–10 minutes until lightly browned.','Add {{stock|0.18747656542932134}}, cover and simmer for 25–35 minutes until soft. Press the carrots and cooking liquid through a sieve into a bowl.','Melt {{butter|0.5}} in the empty pan, stir in {{flour}} and cook for 2 minutes. Gradually whisk in the carrot mixture and {{stock|0.8125234345706787}}. Add {{salt}} and {{pepper}} and simmer for 10 minutes.']+eggfinish(),'The source 2⅔ L stock is rounded to 2667 ml; about 500 ml is used first. Source butter is interpreted as 30 g using the book-style 20 g tablespoon and divided between browning and roux. The undefined cream part becomes 100 ml. These choices are explicit modern estimates.','Soups')
