r=add(130,'Vegetariansk Morotpuré with Leek and Shallot',10,150,'Grated carrots, leek and shallot simmer slowly in water before a browned roux and finishing butter enrich the soup.',[carrot(1000),I('shallot',30,'g','peeled shallot','Use the same weight of onion.'),I('leek',150,'g','trimmed leek, thoroughly rinsed','Use the same weight of onion.'),water(2500),water(1000,'blanch'),butter(28),flour(24),salt(5),dict(pepper(),name='ground white pepper'),I('finish',5,'g','cold unsalted butter','Use 5 g a block-style dairy-free butter alternative.'),bread(200),I('cheese',100,'g','sliced firm cheese','Use the same weight of a firm dairy-free cheese.')],['Briefly blanch {{carrot}} in {{blanch}} for 3 minutes, drain and cool just enough to handle. Grate coarsely. Thinly slice {{shallot}} and {{leek}}.','Combine the grated carrots, shallot, leek, {{water}}, {{salt}} and {{pepper}}. Cover loosely and simmer for 90–120 minutes until very soft. Press through a coarse sieve into a bowl.','Melt {{butter}} in the saucepan, stir in {{flour}} and cook for 3–4 minutes until light golden. Gradually whisk in the carrot mixture and simmer for 10–15 minutes, stirring.','Take off the heat and stir in {{finish}}. Make open sandwiches from {{bread}} and {{cheese}} and serve alongside.'],'Matching transcriptions are consolidated. Carrots are already peeled for the modern blanch-and-grate sequence. The extra teaspoon of finishing butter is counted separately; bread and cheese amounts are supplied. A light rather than browned roux is retained as a named method.','Soups')
