r=add(131,'Vegetariansk Morotpuré with Rice and Cream',6,160,'Carrots and shallots make a rich smooth soup with an egg-cream finish and separately cooked rice served alongside.',[carrot(1000),I('shallot',90,'g','peeled shallots','Use the same weight of onion.'),butter(100),water(2000),flour(40),salt(3),dict(pepper(),name='ground white pepper'),yolks(2),cream(200),rice(80),water(1000,'ricewater'),I('ricesalt',7.5,'g','fine salt for the rice cooking water','Reduce or omit.')],['Dice {{carrot}} and slice {{shallot}}. Melt {{butter|0.4}} in a saucepan and brown the vegetables lightly for 8–10 minutes.','Add {{water}}, {{salt}} and {{pepper}}. Cover loosely and simmer gently for about 2 hours until completely soft, adding small splashes of water if needed to prevent drying. Press through a sieve into a bowl.','Melt {{butter|0.4}} in the empty pan, stir in {{flour}} and cook for 2 minutes. Gradually whisk in the sieved carrot mixture and simmer for 5 minutes.','Meanwhile, rinse {{rice}}. Bring {{ricewater}} and {{ricesalt}} to a boil, add the rice and simmer for 15–20 minutes until tender. Drain well and keep hot.']+eggfinish()+['Take the soup off the heat and stir in {{butter|0.2}}. Serve the cooked rice in a separate warm dish for spooning into the soup.'],'Four equivalent transcriptions are consolidated. The original recipe 275 and its recipe 266 cross-reference were checked. Butter is 100 g, not the corrupt hectoliter translation, divided 40/40/20 g. The word karott means a serving dish, not a carrot. Rice mass and shallot weight are modern estimates; the original six generous portions are retained.','Soups')
