r=add(78,'Carrots au Beurre (Butter-Warmed Carrot Batons)',4,50,'Carrots are boiled whole, cut into long batons and gently warmed in a generous amount of butter.',[carrot(500),water(1200),salt(3),butter(60),pepper()],['Put {{carrot}} whole in a saucepan with {{water}} and {{salt}}. Bring to a simmer and cook for 20–35 minutes until tender. Drain and cool just enough to handle.','Quarter lengthwise and cut into approximately 7 cm lengths. Melt {{butter}} over low heat, add the carrots and {{pepper}} and gently turn for 3–5 minutes until hot and coated, without browning.'],'The source calls for a large piece of butter; the modern batch uses 60 g for 500 g carrots. Cooking whole before cutting and the generous butter finish distinguish it from simple diced boiled carrots.')
