r=add(116,'Glaserade Morötter (Boiled Then Glazed Carrots)',4,45,'Small carrots are boiled until tender, peeled and rolled in a simple butter-sugar glaze.',[I('carrot',12,'','small whole carrots, about 40 g each','Use about 480 g larger carrots, cut into similar-sized pieces; peeling before cooking is easier with cut carrots.'),water(1000),salt(3),butter(28),sugar(8)],['Scrub {{carrot}} thoroughly. Bring {{water}} and {{salt}} to a boil, add the carrots and simmer for 15–25 minutes until tender. Drain and cool just enough to handle, then gently scrape off the skins.','Melt {{butter}} with {{sugar}} in a wide pan over low heat. Add the warm carrots and turn gently for 3–5 minutes until glossy. Do not let the sugar burn. Serve warm.'],'The source twelve small carrots are specified at roughly 40 g each; missing water and salt are supplied. This boil-then-glaze method stays distinct from the butter-first reduction method.')
r=add(117,'Glaserade Morötter (Butter-Braised Glazed Carrots)',6,40,'Small carrots sauté in butter, then simmer until their sweet cooking liquid reduces to a glossy coating.',[carrot(600),butter(60),salt(5),sugar(20),water(400),parsley()],['Choose small carrots for {{carrot}} and halve or quarter lengthwise to make even pieces. Pat dry.','Melt {{butter}} in a wide saucepan, add the carrots, {{salt}} and {{sugar}}, and sauté gently for 3–5 minutes without dark browning.','Add {{water}}, cover and simmer for 15–25 minutes until nearly tender. Uncover and simmer for 5–10 minutes until the liquid forms a light glaze; turn the carrots gently to coat. Stop before the sugar catches.','Toss with {{parsley}} and serve.'],'Four equivalent Idun transcriptions are consolidated. The ambiguous four parts water is resolved by companion texts specifying 4 dcl, or 400 ml. A liter of small carrots becomes a disclosed 600 g prepared weight. Parsley is selected from the optional finish. Older-carrot preblanching is a named variation.')
variant(r,'older-carrots','Preblanched mature carrots',copy.deepcopy(r['ingredients'])+[water(1000,'blanchwater'),I('blanchsalt',3,'g','fine salt for blanching water','Reduce or omit.')],['Cut {{carrot}} into even 1 cm thick batons. Put in {{blanchwater}} with {{blanchsalt}}, bring to a boil and simmer for 5 minutes. Drain well.']+r['steps'][1:])
r=add(121,'Kokta Morötter with Butter Water-Bath Finish',4,50,'Whole carrots are boiled, peeled and sliced, then gently warmed with sugar and cold butter over a water bath.',[dict(carrot(500),name='whole unpeeled carrots, scrubbed clean'),water(500),salt(5),sugar(5),butter(20)],['Put {{carrot}} in a snug saucepan with {{water}} and {{salt}}. Bring to a boil, cover and simmer for 20–35 minutes until tender when pierced with a small knife. Add water if needed to keep the pan from drying.','Drain and cool just enough to handle. Scrape off the skins, cut into small pieces and place in a heatproof bowl.','Sprinkle with {{sugar}} and dot with {{butter}}. Set the bowl over a saucepan of gently simmering water, keeping its base above the water. Cover loosely and warm for 5–10 minutes, stirring once, until hot and the butter melts. Serve immediately.'],'Three identical source transcriptions are consolidated. Source metric amounts are retained. The unclear whisk tenderness test becomes a knife test, and the water-bath setup is made explicit.')
r=add(127,'Stuvade Morötter with Parsley and Finishing Butter',6,45,'Carrot batons are coated in a roux sauce made from their cooking liquid, then finished with parsley and cold butter.',[carrot(750),water(500),salt(5),sugar(5),butter(40),flour(40),I('finish',10,'g','cold unsalted butter','Use the same weight of a block-style dairy-free butter alternative.'),parsley(12)],['Cut {{carrot}} into even 1 cm thick batons. Bring {{water}}, {{salt}} and {{sugar}} to a boil in a snug pan, add the carrots and cook covered for 15–25 minutes until tender. Add small splashes of water if needed.','Drain into a bowl, reserving the cooking liquid. Add drinking water to the reserved liquid as needed to restore the original cooking-water volume.','Melt {{butter}} in the saucepan, stir in {{flour}} and cook for 2 minutes. Gradually whisk in the reserved cooking liquid and simmer for 5 minutes until smooth.','Fold in the carrots, bring to a gentle simmer and take off the heat. Stir in {{finish}} and {{parsley}} and serve.'],'Two equivalent Idun transcriptions are consolidated. The source 450–500 ml cooking liquid is fixed at 500 ml by replacing evaporation losses; it is not an extra ingredient. Butter for the roux and cold finish remains separate. The source milk option is preserved.')
variant(r,'milk','Milk sauce',copy.deepcopy(r['ingredients'])+[milk(500)],[r['steps'][0],'Drain and discard the cooking liquid.','Melt {{butter}} in the saucepan, stir in {{flour}} and cook for 2 minutes. Gradually whisk in {{milk}} and simmer for 5 minutes until smooth.',r['steps'][3]])
r=add(128,'Stuvade Morötter (Carrots Braised in Parsley Sauce)',6,40,'Carrot strips start in butter and cook directly in a lightly thickened parsley sauce.',[carrot(1000),butter(28),flour(24),water(500),parsley(16),sugar(5),salt(3)],['Cut {{carrot}} into strips about 5 cm long and 1 cm wide. Melt {{butter}} in a wide saucepan, add the carrots and cook gently for 3 minutes without browning.','Sprinkle over {{flour}} and stir for 1 minute. Gradually stir in {{water}}, {{salt}} and {{sugar}}. Cover and simmer for 20–30 minutes, stirring regularly, until tender; add a little water if the sauce begins to catch.','Add {{parsley}} for the final 2 minutes and serve with the sauce.'],'The source kilogram of carrots is retained. Missing water, sugar and salt amounts are supplied. This direct butter-and-flour braise is distinct from boiling, draining and preparing a separate roux sauce.')
